  "raw_text": "53\n\nBrit krikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto break bread\n \n/ partir el pan\n\nBrit pîs\n \n–\n \npiece of bread\n \n/ pedazo de pan\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nlfb48\n):\n \nPliskam pali, brit pîs kum aik\n \n–\n \nPlease give me a piece of bread\n \n/ Por favor dame un pedazo de pan)\n\nBritbrit\n \n(\ndict\n;\n \nBrit-brit\n-bc\n)\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nguava\n \n/ guayaba\n\nBritput\n \n(\nbc\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nbreadfruit\n \n/ fruta de pan\n\nBrukwaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto complain, to murmur, to protest\n \n/ quejarse, murmurar, protestar\n\nBrukwaia aisaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto complain, to murmur, to protest\n \n/ quejarse, murmurar, protestar\n\nBrukwan lâka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ncomplaint, murmuring, protest, argument\n \n/ queja, murmullo, protesta, discusión\n\nBrukwan âpu hilp munaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto help without complaint, to help without protest, to cooperate\n \n/ ayudar sin\nquejas, ayudar sin protestar, cooperar\n\nBrum\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nbroom\n \n/ escoba\n\nBuaia\n \n(a/t:\n \nBuwaia\n) (v-intrans; trans:\n \nBukaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto be standing, to stand up, to rise, to be raised, to be resuscitated, to get\nup\n \n/ estar de pie, pararse, levantarse, resucitar\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nlfb38\n):\n \nTihmia ra Samson buan, ...\n \n–\n \nIn the night, Samson got up, ...\n \n/ En la noche, Sansón se levantó, ...)\n\nBapi buaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto stand up to, to stand up for, to endure\n \n/ resistir, defender, aguantar\n\nBan bapi buaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto endure, to continue to endure, to continue to stand up to, to remain firm, to\nremain steadfast\n \n/ aguantar, continuar aguantando, continuar resistiendo, continuar defendiendo,\nmantenerse firme, permanecer firme\n\nBapi buanka l\nâ\nka\n \n(\nwqu\n-\n10/19\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nendurance\n \n/ aguante\n\nKasak bapi buaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto remain firm and true, to remain steadfast and true, to remain faithful and true\n\n/ permanecer firme y verdadero, permanecer firme y verdadero, permanecer fiel y verdadero\n\nMapara bapi buaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto stand up against, to stand up to\n \n/ enfrentarse a\n\nBabura\n \n(n\n-\nagent/s\n-\nagente)\n \n–\n \none who rises, one who opposes\n \n/\n \nu\nno que se levanta, uno que se opone\n\nMapa babura, Mapara\n \nbabura\n \n(n\n-\nagent/s\n-\nagente)\n \n–\n \nrebel, person opposing, one who rises against\n \n/\n\nrebelde, persona que se opone, uno que se levanta\n \nen\n \ncontra\n\nMapara Babura\n \n–\n \nOpposer\n \n(the meaning of Satan) / Opositor (el significado de Satanás)\n\nB\nû\ni\n \n(2) (v\n-\npresent\n \nparticiple of / participio presente de:\n \nBuaia\n)\n \n–\n \nstanding, standing up, raising, resuscitating\n \n/ de\n\npie, levantando, resucitando\n\nKli buaia\n \n(v-intrans; trans:\n \nKli bukaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto stand again, to be resurrected, to be raised\n \n/ estar de pie otra vez, ser\nresucitado, resucitar\n\n(Ex/Ej(\ndb-Apastil Nani Sturka 24:15\n):\n \nPruan nani ba kli buaia sa\n \n–\n \nthe dead are to rise again\n \n/ los muertos van a resucitar)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nlfb48\n):\n \nBaha piua kat, pruan kumi sin kli buras kan.\n \n–\n \nUp to that time, not one dead person was (had been) raised.\n \n/\nHasta ese momento, ni una persona muerta fue (había sido) resucitada.)\n\nKli buaia lâka bîla kaikanka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nhope of the resurrection\n \n/ esperanza de la resurrección\n\nKli buan lâka\n \n(a/t:\n \nKli buaia lâka\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nresurrection\n \n/ resurrección\n\n(Construct:\n \nKli buanka l\nâ\nka\n)\n\n(\nEx/Ej:\n \nJisas kli buanka l\nâ\nka ba\n \n–\n \nJesus\n’ resurrection\n \n/ la resurrección de Jesús\n)\n\nMapa buaia, Mapara buaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto oppose, to rebel, to stand up against\n \n/ oponerse, rebelarse, enfrentarse\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nhf\n-\n16\n):\n \nYaptikam ba piu bani maipa buisa\n \n–\n \nYour mother always opposes me\n \n/ Tu madre siempre se opone a mi\n)\n\nMapa babura, Mapara babura\n \n(n\n-\nagent/s\n-\nagente)\n \n–\n \nrebel, person opposing, one who rises against\n \n/\n\nrebelde, persona que se opone, uno que se levanta\n \nen\n \ncontra\n\nMapara Babura\n \n–\n \nOpposer\n \n(the meaning of Satan) / Opositor (el significado de Satanás)\n\nMapara bapi buaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto stand up against, to stand up to\n \n/ enfrentarse a\n\nMapa buanka\n, Mapara\n \nbuanka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nopposition, rebellion, revolt\n \n/ oposición, rebelión, revuelta\n\nMapa buan l\nâ\nka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nopposition\n, rebellion, revolt\n \n/ oposición, rebelión, revuelta\n\nNahki buram?\n \n(exp)\n \n–\n \nHow did you rise?\n \n/ ¿Cómo te levantaste?\n\n(Note\n/Nota\n:\n \nNahki\n \nlalawram\n?\n \nis a similar expression\n \n/\n \nNahki lalawram?\n \nes una expresión similar\n)\n\nPrura wina buanka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \n(the) raising from death, resurrection\n \n/ (la) resurrección de la muerte, la resurrección\n\nTit buaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto rise instantly, to rise suddenly, to stand up instantly, to stand up suddenly\n \n/ levantarse al\ninstante, levantarse de repente, ponerse de pie al instante, ponerse de pie de repente\n\n(Ex/Ej(\ndb-Aiseya 48:3\n):\n \nTit bui daukri bara baku dukia nani ba pain takan.\n \n–\n \nnwt\n:\n \nSuddenly I took action, and they came\nabout.\n \n/\n \ntnm\n: De repente actué, y se realizaron.\n)\n\nBuhkaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto light with a torch\n \n/\n \nalumbrar\n \ncon una antorcha",
